.TH FASTVM-API 1 "March 2026" "fastvm-api 1.0.0" "FastVM Manual"
.SH NAME
fastvm\-api \- REST API server for FastVM (runs on a backend host)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastvm\-api
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR proxmox|firecracker ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastvm\-api
is a Go HTTP server that runs on the VM backend host and provides a REST API
for VM lifecycle management. It can manage Proxmox VMs or Firecracker
microVMs behind the same client API.
.PP
Remote clients (the
.B fastvm
CLI, CI/CD pipelines, AI agents) connect over HTTP.
.SH BACKEND SIZING
Firecracker follows the upstream Firecracker machine\-config API and supports
at most 32 vCPUs per microVM. Use Firecracker for fast create/clone/destroy
workflows and for scale\-out across multiple microVMs.
.PP
Use Proxmox for one large compile VM, including 64\-120+ vCPU requests.
FastVM preserves the requested Proxmox VM core count, but caps virtio
.B net0.queues
at 64 because Proxmox rejects larger NIC queue counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port PORT
HTTP listen port. Default: 8090.
.TP
.B \-\-backend proxmox|firecracker
VM backend implementation. Default: firecracker.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
State directory with vms.json and users.json. Default: /var/lib/fastvm.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-host HOSTNAME
Public hostname or IP that users should SSH to for port\-forwarded VM access.
This value appears in the
.B ssh_command
field of API responses (e.g., "ssh \-p 60000 ubuntu@HOSTNAME").
Default: the machine's hostname.
.TP
.B \-\-firecracker\-install\-dir DIR
Firecracker install directory. Default: /opt/fastvm-microvm.
.TP
.B \-\-firecracker\-bin PATH
Path to firecrackerctl. Default: <install-dir>/bin/firecrackerctl.
.TP
.B \-\-firecracker\-template NAME
Default Firecracker rootfs template name. Default: 9013.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FASTVM_BACKEND
Backend implementation: proxmox or firecracker. Default: firecracker.
.TP
.B FASTVM_STATE_DIR
State directory (same as \-\-state\-dir).
.TP
.B FASTVM_SSH_HOST
Public hostname/IP for SSH proxy commands (same as \-\-ssh\-host).
.TP
.B FASTVM_DEFAULT_TEMPLATE
Proxmox template VMID used when create requests omit the template field.
Default: 9012.
.TP
.B FASTVM_FIRECRACKER_INSTALL_DIR
Firecracker install directory.
.TP
.B FASTVM_FIRECRACKER_DEFAULT_TEMPLATE
Default Firecracker rootfs template name.
.TP
.B FASTVM_FIRECRACKER_SSH_USER
Guest SSH user for Firecracker responses. Default: root.
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.SS Health & Status
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/health
Returns {"status":"ok"}. Use for liveness probes.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/status
System overview: total VMs, user count, per\-user network allocations.
.SS VM Lifecycle
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/vms
Create VMs. Body:
.nf
  {"user":"X", "count":N, "memory":4096, "cores":2,
   "template":9012, "ssh_key":"/path/to/key.pub"}
.fi
Returns created VMs with deterministic IPs immediately.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/vms[?user=X]
List VMs, optionally filtered by user.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/vms/{vmid}
Get single VM details.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/vms/{vmid}
Queue destruction of a single VM. The VM is removed from FastVM state
immediately; backend cleanup may continue asynchronously.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/users/{user}/vms
Queue destruction of all VMs for a user. Cleans up FastVM state and networking
when the last VM is removed; backend cleanup may continue asynchronously.
.SS Snapshot
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/vms/{vmid}/snapshot
Convert a VM into a Proxmox template. The VM is stopped, its SSH proxy removed,
and it becomes an immutable template suitable for cloning. The VM is unregistered
from active state. Returns the template VMID for use with
.BR "POST /api/v1/vms" " (template field)" .
.PP
Response:
.nf
  {"ok": true, "data": {"vmid": "60000",
   "message": "VM 60000 converted to template. Use -t 60000 to clone from it."}}
.fi
.SS Convergence
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/converge
Keep one VM, destroy the rest. Body: {"user":"X", "keep_vmid":"60001"}.
.SS SSH Proxy
When a VM is created, the API automatically starts a
.B socat
listener on port = VMID that forwards to the VM's internal SSH port (22).
This allows external users to SSH into VMs without needing hypervisor access
or knowing internal IPs.
.PP
The proxy binds to 0.0.0.0 on the backend host. PID files are stored in
.IR /var/lib/fastvm/proxy/<vmid>.pid .
On VM destruction, the proxy is stopped automatically.
On API startup, orphan proxies (from crashed runs) are cleaned up.
.PP
VM responses include
.B ssh_port
(= VMID) and
.B ssh_command
(e.g., "ssh \-p 60000 ubuntu@host") fields.
.PP
Requirements:
.B socat
must be installed. Ports 60000\-60999 must be open in any firewall.
.SH RESPONSE FORMAT
.nf
{
  "ok": true|false,
  "data": { ... },
  "error": "message" | null
}
.fi
.SH DEPLOYMENT
The API server is designed to run on the backend host as a systemd service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Unit]
Description=FastVM API Server
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/fastvm-api --port 8090
Restart=always
User=root

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
.fi
.RE
.PP
It needs root or equivalent permissions for the selected backend: qm on
Proxmox, or firecrackerctl and networking setup on Firecracker hosts.
